      "writtenOn": "2022-05-10T10:28:13Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "I have often found that adding data and even behavior to the tag results in smaller and cleaner code. You just have to decide whether the tag is a struct that is copied everywhere, or a pointer to a struct that is shared. If you have lots of data in the tag it is better to pass around a pointer to it but you have to make sure that you don\u0027t accidentally try and change the contents as that would affect every dependency that uses it.",
